WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.840
How does a cell decide it can afford to grow?

2
00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:09.460
Growth is expensive.

3
00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:14.740
Making protein uses amino acids and much of a cell's ATP.

4
00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:23.340
So a kinase called mTOR, inside a complex named mTORC1, asks two questions.

5
00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:26.980
It switches on only when both get a yes.

6
00:00:27.883 --> 00:00:31.323
The first question: has the body said grow?

7
00:00:31.323 --> 00:00:40.103
A growth factor switches on Akt. Akt phosphorylates a protein of the TSC complex,

8
00:00:40.103 --> 00:00:42.703
which takes the complex out of action.

9
00:00:43.223 --> 00:00:49.583
The TSC complex is a GAP, an off switch for a small GTPase called Rheb.

10
00:00:49.583 --> 00:00:52.863
So Rheb stays loaded with GTP.

11
00:00:52.863 --> 00:00:58.223
Rheb with GTP is the direct activator of mTORC1.

12
00:00:59.017 --> 00:01:02.137
The second question: are there amino acids?

13
00:01:02.897 --> 00:01:04.937
The expected answer was a receptor.

14
00:01:05.617 --> 00:01:08.397
It was the Rags, small GTPases.

15
00:01:09.057 --> 00:01:12.377
They do not raise the kinase activity of mTORC1.

16
00:01:12.897 --> 00:01:18.737
They move it. Without amino acids, mTORC1 stays spread through the cytoplasm.

17
00:01:19.517 --> 00:01:24.357
With them, it gathers on the surface of the lysosome, the cell's acidic digestive

18
00:01:24.357 --> 00:01:28.397
compartment. That surface is where it is thought to meet Rheb.

19
00:01:29.217 --> 00:01:35.177
Rheb with GTP can activate only a complex that has been brought to it.

20
00:01:35.857 --> 00:01:38.277
Growth factors set whether Rheb is on.

21
00:01:39.317 --> 00:01:42.057
Amino acids set whether the complex is delivered.

22
00:01:42.857 --> 00:01:44.417
This is an AND gate.

23
00:01:45.197 --> 00:01:51.337
With both, mTORC1 acts on proteins that control the first step of making protein.

24
00:01:52.097 --> 00:01:56.317
With no growth factor, Rheb is off, so the complex stays off.

25
00:01:56.317 --> 00:02:01.357
With no amino acids, the complex leaves the lysosome and stays off.

26
00:02:02.217 --> 00:02:04.337
A third gauge reads energy.

27
00:02:04.977 --> 00:02:10.257
A healthy cell keeps ATP nearly constant, so ATP is a poor alarm.

28
00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:18.357
AMP moves most. With round numbers, when ATP falls by a tenth, AMP rises almost

29
00:02:18.357 --> 00:02:23.037
fourfold. So the kinase AMPK reads AMP.

30
00:02:23.737 --> 00:02:28.077
Once on, AMPK makes the TSC complex more active.

31
00:02:28.617 --> 00:02:30.457
That drains Rheb of GTP.

32
00:02:30.457 --> 00:02:35.077
It also phosphorylates Raptor, which inhibits mTORC1.

33
00:02:36.077 --> 00:02:40.297
Energy can veto growth, even when growth factors and amino acids are present.

34
00:02:41.167 --> 00:02:43.427
You can now predict a cell.

35
00:02:44.127 --> 00:02:48.827
When fed, every input says yes, and protein synthesis runs.

36
00:02:49.747 --> 00:02:55.527
With no amino acids, mTORC1 leaves the lysosome, and translation slows.

37
00:02:56.647 --> 00:02:59.707
With no energy, AMPK switches on.

38
00:03:00.187 --> 00:03:04.567
It shuts mTORC1 off, even when everything else is present.

39
00:03:05.427 --> 00:03:10.467
Keep this rule: two yeses to grow, and low energy can veto them.
